course: dictionary
lesson: 11843
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing. The word bloated can mean swollen, full after eating, or too big with too much in it. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which are its context.
explain: «After the big dinner, Sam felt so bloated that he had to lie down.» Sam ate too much, so bloated means uncomfortably full, like a tummy stuffed after eating. The clue is the big dinner.
explain: «The dead fish lay on the beach, bloated and swollen with gas.» Here bloated means swollen and bigger than normal, because of gas. The clue is swollen. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check.
fact: Bloated means swollen and bigger than normal, often because of air, gas or liquid.
fact: Bloated can mean uncomfortably full after eating or drinking, as in «I feel bloated».
fact: Bloated can also mean too big, with too much in it, as in «a bloated budget».
fact: «Bloated» is also the past form of the verb bloat, which means to swell up.
fact: When a word has several meanings, the sentence tells you which one the writer means.
exercise: «After the big dinner, Sam felt so bloated that he had to lie down.» What does bloated mean here? | Too big, with too much in it | Very thin and weak | Swollen with gas | *Uncomfortably full after eating
exercise: «The dead fish lay on the beach, bloated and swollen.» What does bloated mean here? | Cold and wet | Too big, with too much spent | Feeling full after a meal | *Swollen and bigger than normal
exercise: «The company had a bloated budget, with money spent on things it did not need.» What does bloated mean here? | *Too big, with too much in it | Empty and tiny | Swollen with gas | Feeling full after eating
test: «Mum said the balloon looked bloated, so she let a little air out.» What does bloated mean here? | Too big, with too much spent | *Swollen and bigger than normal | Bright and shiny | Uncomfortably full after eating
test: Ellie says bloated always means fat. Is she right? | Yes, it always means fat | No, it can mean swollen, full after eating, or too big with too much in it | Yes, but only after dinner | *No, but it can mean swollen, full after eating, or too big with too much in it
exam: Read this: «The bloated software took up too much space on the computer.» Which meaning of bloated fits best, and why? | Full after eating, because the computer ate the space | Swollen with gas, because computers can puff up | Very thin, because the software was small | *Too big, with too much in it, because the software is too large
